WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
During an emergency it is normal to experience a rush of adrenaline which can narrow your focus

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:11.920
onto a specific task and limit your ability to process surroundings. Remember, slow is smooth

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:19.840
and smooth is fast. We want controlled action, not panic. Look at this picture on the screen.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.480
This is a potential emergency. What do you see? What would you do first? Should you move them?

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:33.279
In a situation like this, scene safety is your absolute priority. Take a moment to pause and

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:38.799
look around. You need to check for hazards like traffic, fire, electricity, or even aggressive

00:00:38.799 --> 00:00:44.320
animals. If the scene is unsafe, stay back and wait for professionals like firefighters or police

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:51.520
to secure the area. You can't help if you're hurt. A question that often comes up is, should I move

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:57.279
them? The answer is only if the scene is unsafe or if you must move them to perform life-saving

00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:03.360
care. For example, it is always okay to move someone to perform CPR. While we want to minimize

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.400
movement for things like suspected spine injuries, if there is an immediate danger like fire or

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.519
oncoming traffic, it is best to move them to safety.

